faqHeading: "Questions about cost and commitment."
faqClass: "sec-alt tint-green"
faq:
  - q: "Why private pay rather than insurance?"
    a: "<p>Practically: it means no diagnosis requirement, no cap on the number of sessions, no waiting on authorizations, and no pressure to shape your child's goals to fit a billing category. It also means I can work in your home and out in the community, which many plans don't cover well.</p><p>The trade-off is real and worth saying plainly: the cost sits with your family rather than an insurer. For some families that's the reason this works, and for some it's the reason it doesn't. Either is a fine answer, and talking to me costs nothing precisely so you can find out which before you spend a penny.</p>"
  - q: "Would I get a superbill to claim back?"
    a: "<p>Yes, on request. A superbill is an itemized receipt with the codes an insurer needs. You pay me for the session, then submit the superbill to your insurer yourself and claim against your out-of-network benefits.</p><p>What comes back depends entirely on your plan — some families are reimbursed a good portion, some nothing at all. It is worth calling your insurer before you start and asking specifically about out-of-network occupational therapy, and about your out-of-network deductible. I can't promise a reimbursement, only the paperwork to ask for one.</p>"
  - q: "How many sessions will we need?"
    a: "There's no set answer, and I'd be suspicious of anyone who gave you one before meeting your child. Some families come weekly for a stretch and stop. Others check in every few weeks, or come back when something changes. We decide the rhythm together after the first session and revisit it whenever it stops fitting."
  - q: "Can I stop, or take a break?"
    a: "Any time, and without explaining yourself. There's no package to buy and nothing to cancel out of. Families pause for holidays, for illness, for money, or because things are going well — all normal."
  - q: "What's your cancellation policy?"
    a: "Sessions need to be cancelled at least 24 hours in advance. Inside 24 hours the full session fee is due — the time is held for your child and can't usually be filled at short notice. Life happens, though, so talk to me rather than assuming the worst."
  - q: "Do you take on families outside East Jefferson County?"
    a: "<p>There are two answers, because there are two ways of working.</p><p><b>In person</b>, the service area is a real limit rather than a preference — I'm driving to you, so East Jefferson County is genuinely how far it reaches. If you're just outside it, ask; it's often workable.</p><p><b>Remotely</b>, the reach is the whole Olympic Peninsula, at the same rate, for both direct sessions and family consulting. So being outside driving range doesn't rule it out — it changes what the sessions look like. <a href=\"/in-home-ot/#remote\">More on remote sessions</a>."
---

